{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 78, :comments ["<b>Ahira son of Enan.</b> It alludes, by way of the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Sifrei Deuteronomy 33:23) on the verse ״שְׂבַע רָצוֹן״ — which teaches that Naphtali was satisfied with his portion in seas, in fish, in pergolae — ״וּמָלֵא בִּרְכַּת ה׳״ the Sea of Ginosar, end quote. And this is the meaning of <b>Ahira</b> [\"my brother is evil\"]: that the portion of his brothers was evil in his eyes in comparison to his portion, and his eye was full from the portion that fell to him in the lot."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:46.572481053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}